          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What HbA1c target does guidance describe, and is there one number everybody uses?",
          "answer": "Clinical guidance on HbA1c targets for diabetes management varies, and there is no single, universally accepted number.\n\nSome guidelines suggest 7% as a default target, while also emphasizing that this should be individualized for each person. Other guidelines prioritize an individualized range and do not provide a specific headline figure. This approach aims to prevent the target from being applied too rigidly.\n\nGuidance also notes that severe hypoglycemia is a reason to relax an HbA1c goal rather than to strictly pursue it (National diabetes association standards of care (educational summary), \"Type 2 diabetes: glycemic targets and monitoring intervals\").\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
